# EtMotionSwap

A dumb, props-driven component that crossfades between two **always-mounted** layers using only `opacity` and `translateX` / `translateY` — no mount/unmount, 100% UI thread.

## When to use

Use `EtMotionSwap` when:
- You want a smooth directional swap between two views (e.g. amount-mode hero, sub-line figures).
- Both layers are cheap to keep mounted (counters, text rows).
- You want zero JS-thread involvement in the animation.

Do **not** use when the two layers have significantly different heights — the container is sized to `first` in normal flow, and `second` is absolutely positioned inside it. Both layers should be the same height (or the same flex height in context).

## API

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `showSecond` | `boolean` | — | `true` → second layer visible, first exits |
| `axis` | `'x' \| 'y'` | — | Direction of the slide (x = left/right, y = up/down) |
| `distance` | `number` | `14` | px travelled by entering/exiting layer |
| `opacityOnly` | `boolean` | `false` | Fade in place only — no directional translate |
| `rasterizeLayers` | `boolean` | `false` | Snapshot each layer to a hardware texture before fading |
| `first` | `ReactNode` | — | Default/primary content |
| `second` | `ReactNode` | — | Alternate content |
| `timingConfig` | `WithTimingConfig` | `{ duration: 220 }` | Timing override |
| `style` | `StyleProp<ViewStyle>` | — | Container style |
| `testID` | `string` | — | Test identifier |

## Animation mechanics

A single `progress` shared value (0 → 1) drives interpolated properties on the UI thread:

- `first`: `opacity` 1→0; optional `translate[axis]` 0→`-distance` (skipped when `opacityOnly`)
- `second`: `opacity` 0→1; optional `translate[axis]` `+distance`→0 (skipped when `opacityOnly`)

Animation starts in `useLayoutEffect` so the fade begins on the same frame as `showSecond` changes.

Reversing (`showSecond` false→true then back) mirrors automatically.

## Layout strategy

`first` renders in normal flow to anchor the container size. `second` sits in `StyleSheet.absoluteFill` centered with `alignItems/justifyContent: center`. This works without measurement when both layers have the same height.

## Usage examples

```tsx
// Horizontal hero swap
<EtMotionSwap
  axis="x"
  showSecond={amountMode === 'units'}
  first={<ExecutionAmountDisplay rawAmountStr={dollarsStr} />}
  second={<ExecutionAmountDisplay rawAmountStr={unitsStr} />}
/>

// Vertical sub-line figure swap
<EtMotionSwap
  axis="y"
  showSecond={amountMode === 'dollars'}
  first={<AmountSublineFigure {...unitsProps} />}
  second={<AmountSublineFigure {...dollarsProps} />}
/>
```
